quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  2,58,"And (remember) when We said: ‘Enter this town,* and eat from it freely wherever you wish, but enter prostrating at the gate (of the town), and say: ‘We repent (for all of our sins),’ that We may forgive your sins. And We shall soon increase the virtuous (in their rewards).’"
  2,59,"But the wrongdoers substituted a different word from the one they were told. So, We sent down upon the wrongdoers a plague (as a punishment) from heaven because of their persistent disobeying."
  2,60,"(Remember) when Musa (Moses) prayed for water for his people, We said (to him): ‘strike the rock with your staff.’ Thereby, twelve springs gushed from it. Each tribe came to know its drinking place. (We said): ‘Eat and drink of Allah’s provision, but do not act sinfully in the land, causing corruption.’"
  2,61,"And (remember) when you said, ‘O Musa (Moses), we cannot bear to eat only one kind of food (i.e. manna and quails), so pray to your Lord to bring out for us some of the earth’s produce, its green herbs, its cucumbers, its garlic, its lentils and its onions.’ ‘What!’ He answered, ‘Would you exchange what is better for what is worse? Go down to any city. There you shall find all that you have asked for.’ So they were struck with disgrace and poverty. And they incurred the wrath of Allah because they persistently rejected the signs of Allah and killed the Prophets unjustly. All this was because they used to disobey and would (always) commit transgressions."
